From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:02:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] msm8996-common: def_device_font_scale 1.15 for the 420
 dpi panel

Since settings version 224 SettingsProvider seeds Settings.System.FONT_SCALE from
R.dimen.def_device_font_scale (handleDefaultFontScale) and records it as
DEFAULT_DEVICE_FONT_SCALE for "Reset settings", so the device overlay is the whole change; no
framework patch is needed on this branch. 420 dpi buys 548 dp of width at the cost of physically
small text on 5.7 inches; 1.15 is the second step of the SettingsLib ladder so it stays a normal,
movable selection in Settings. Only fresh data picks it up: an existing /data already past
version 224 keeps its font_scale.
---
 .../base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
index dd46637c..324b3b06 100644
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SettingsProvider/res/values/defaults.xml
@@ -21,4 +21,11 @@
     <bool name="def_screen_brightness_automatic_mode">true</bool>
     <!-- Default screen brightness, from 0 to 255. 87 is 34%. -->
     <integer name="def_screen_brightness">53</integer>
+
+    <!-- Text one notch up, to compensate for shipping the panel at 420 dpi. That reports this
+         1440x2560 screen as 548 dp wide, which is the room dense layouts need but leaves text
+         physically small on 5.7 inches. 1.15 is the second step of the SettingsLib ladder
+         (0.85 / 1.0 / 1.15 / 1.30), so Settings shows it as a normal selection the user can move
+         either way. Applied by SettingsProvider's handleDefaultFontScale on fresh data only. -->
+    <item name="def_device_font_scale" format="float" type="dimen">1.15</item>
 </resources>
